<Layout title="About Koursea Blog" description="Learn how Koursea Blog creates practical, source-aware Korea travel guidance for international visitors.">
  <article class="page prose"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE JOURNAL</p><h1>Practical Korea guidance, written for the moment you need it.</h1><p class="lead">Koursea Blog is the editorial companion to Koursea, a zero-login Korea travel platform built for international visitors.</p><h2>What we publish</h2><p>Our guides focus on decisions that generic destination lists often skip: which map app works for a particular journey, how to show a Korean address to a driver, what to confirm before paying, and where rules may change by venue or operator.</p><h2>How we work</h2><p>We compare official instructions, public operator information and practical traveler workflows. Prices, opening hours and policies can change, so every guide encourages readers to confirm time-sensitive details with the relevant official source. We clearly separate practical guidance from medical, legal or financial advice.</p><h2>Our relationship to Koursea</h2><p>The blog explains travel problems in depth. The main <a href="https://www.koursea.com/">Koursea service</a> helps travelers discover places and use field tools such as Korean address cards and local map links.</p></article>
